plugins/aid-orchestrator/defaults/enforcement-registry.yaml:163:  - {id: increment_step_binding,       type: 2, source: "scripts/aid-fsm.sh cmd_increment_step (search: 'IMP-263: step-bound evidence binding')", instruction: "skills/pipeline.md (grep: 'Step-binding block (IMP-263')", severity: blocking, surface: llm-facing, status: active, verdict: ALIGNED, description: "IMP-263: step-verify evidence carrying a binding block is validated against the LIVE plan.json + fsm-state before increment mutates — step_index==current_step, step_id/plan_step_hash==plan steps[N], reviewed_commit==HEAD; a copied/renamed prior verify file is rejected (binding_step_index_mismatch/binding_step_id_mismatch/binding_plan_step_hash_mismatch/binding_wrong_commit/binding_missing_token). Advancement is idempotent + crash-safe via step-transition-ledger.jsonl: the idempotency_token and the current_step bump commit together (ledger append then state write), a replayed token returns status=already_applied without re-advancing, and a crash between the two self-heals on re-invocation (step_transition_recovered) — never a double advance. Stdout is machine-readable (status=advanced|already_applied), never a bare integer. Fail-closed hardening (PM review 2026-07-24): STRICT IS THE DEFAULT — a non-grandfathered run with no binding is rejected without any env; only a genuinely grandfathered created_at (before the deploy threshold) or explicit AID_STEP_BINDING=observe downgrades. A PARTIAL binding (1..4 of the 5 fields) is rejected unconditionally (incomplete_step_binding) — the id/hash/commit checks can no longer be skipped by omitting fields. The crash-recovery self-heal is EVIDENCE-gated: a hand-inserted ledger row {token,from,to} can no longer masquerade as recovery — self-heal runs only when step-<n>-verify.md carries a COMPLETE, live-verified binding matching the ledger token/step/plan/HEAD (predicate _increment_binding_verified); a ledger hit with no valid basis falls through to the fail-closed preconditions, and pure replay (state already at target) stays a safe no-op. Every ledger row written is validated and is a precondition of the current_step bump", test: "scripts/tests/bats/test-aid-fsm.bats (grep: 'IMP-263')"}
