plugins/aid-orchestrator/defaults/enforcement-registry.yaml:1354:    description: "In plan_branch mode both aid-fsm.sh call sites route gate_profile_resolve through _fsm_gate_profile_boundary, which returns boundary=epic; that caps the resolved profile at standard and suppresses the done_phase=release escalation, so an EPIC boundary never starts bats_all. The unbounded result is preserved out-of-band as AID_GATE_PROFILE_FLOOR / --floor-file and recorded by epic-complete as plan_final_required_profile; the cap is applied AFTER the AID_GATE_PROFILE_OVERRIDE layer while the waiver gate still keys off the true (uncapped) risk tier, and the risk_profile_below_required recompute passes the same boundary so a correctly-capped standard run is not measured against an uncapped full. Mode-gated on the committed declared lifecycle manifest only (see plan_mode_single_authority); every 'cannot tell' path degrades toward MORE gates."
