plugins/aid-orchestrator/defaults/enforcement-registry.yaml:1575:    description: "P072 Step 17 (hardened by pre-merge review) — pool eligibility has exactly one authority, and all three consumers use it: aid-bats-parallel-lane.sh, aid-select-tests.sh and aid-test-scheduler.sh all call aid_test_catalog_effective_status_map. The scheduler's approved overlay is an INPUT to that resolver rather than a competing one, and provenance is a floor: an overlay can promote a unit provenance still trusts and can never rescue one it has revoked, because an overlay entry vouches for content it never saw. The authoritative catalog is committed, so a clean clone reproduces the pool. The lane runner reads each unit's effective status from a single catalog snapshot (per-unit re-reads let a concurrent rewrite attach a verdict to a different path than it was made about) and re-hashes every pooled file immediately before dispatch, aborting rather than running content nothing verified. The competing text allowlist is retired to a notice; --allowlist is accepted with a warning that it is not read. The migration carries P071's evidence across with method: migrated_p071_step3, requires each listed path to be its unit's executable source, and REFUSES to migrate a file changed since P071 verified it — hashing edited content into a `safe` status would launder a post-pilot change into fresh-looking evidence."
