plugins/aid-orchestrator/defaults/enforcement-registry.yaml:1673:    description: "P072 Step 26 — a ledger proving no run unit is executed twice within one gate run. FOUR emission paths, not three: the bats lane, the aggregate runner, the scheduler, and — critically — `aid-run-gates.sh` itself for any gate whose command invokes a runner directly. Instrumenting only the three fan-out points would have recorded ONE entry for `gate:bats_fsm` (which runs a file the pool also runs) and reported zero duplicates, certifying as clean the exact defect the ledger exists to detect. There is deliberately NO membership exemption: it was built, and it silenced that same defect, because each dispatch point appends once per execution it actually performs — so two entries under two gate ids are two executions. FAIL-CLOSED throughout (PM review 2026-08-04): once a gate run has opened a ledger, a failed open, a failed append, a named-but-absent ledger file, or a close that cannot be evaluated each fail the whole gate run — the `|| true` that used to wrap the emission paths is gone, and a failed open no longer degrades silently to running unaccounted. A ledger with a gap is indistinguishable from one showing no duplication, so it is never permitted to read as one. The ONE permitted no-op is a dispatch point carrying no ledger path at all — a developer invoking a suite by hand, where there is no accounted run to record against. The scheduler is the fourth real emission path and appends BEFORE launching each unit — a failed append cancels that dispatch, since running a unit no ledger will record is the gap this refuses to produce. Deliberate repeats are declared at the time they happen via `execution_kind` (normal|retry|escalation; `AID_EXECUTION_KIND` declares a whole subprocess, which is how P069 escalation marks itself) and are reported as `deliberate_repeats` instead of failing; the default is `normal`, so an undeclared repeat is still a double execution. Containment NEVER suppresses a finding. P078 amendment (2026-08-10): the bats lane and the scheduler emission paths were deleted with the parallelism machinery — the live emission paths are the aggregate runner and gate_runner_direct; the ledger contract itself is unchanged."
